  "question": {
    "text": "A solution containing $2.675 \\mathrm{~g}$ of $\\mathrm{CoCl}_3 .6 \\mathrm{NH}_3$ (molar mass $=267.5 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ ) is passed through a cation exchanger. The chloride ions obtained in solution were treated with excess of $\\mathrm{AgNO}_3$ to give $4.78 \\mathrm{~g}$ of $\\mathrm{AgCl}$ (molar mass $=143.5 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ ). The formula of the complex is (At. Mass of $\\mathrm{Ag}=108 \\mathrm{u}$ )"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_3$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n $\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}_2\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_4\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}_3\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_3\\right]$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_5\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_2$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{CoCl}_3 .6 \\mathrm{NH}_3 \\rightarrow \\times \\mathrm{Cl}^{-} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{AgNO}_3}{\\longrightarrow} \\times \\mathrm{AgCl} \\downarrow$\n$\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{AgCl})=\\mathrm{x}\\left(\\mathrm{CoCl}_3 .6 \\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)$\n$\\frac{4.78}{143.5}=\\times \\frac{2.675}{267.5} \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{x}=3$\n$\\therefore$ The complex is $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_3$"
  }
}